, and describe the outcome of the task. The entire activity is self-paced and requires a clear audio recording of your walkthrough.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for customer service professionals and support specialists who actively use Salesforce Marketing Cloud. We welcome customer success managers, service desk leads, and marketing support coordinators with hands-on platform experience. You should be comfortable demonstrating your workflows and articulating your process clearly on video.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Record a video walkthrough of a typical Salesforce Marketing Cloud task</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share your screen while navigating the platform interface</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Narrate your process by explaining the steps you take and why</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Highlight the features or tools you use most frequently during your workflow</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Current customer service or support professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience using Salesforce Marketing Cloud</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable recording your screen and providing clear audio commentary</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access to a reliable computer with a working microphone</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$70 per task</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/13a0726b-3698-4f78-82d1-ada921bc6dd6?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe are running a paid study evaluating how customer service teams utilize Salesforce Marketing Cloud in their daily operations. Our goal is to understand real-world campaign execution, audience segmentation, and communication workflows. This research helps map the typical user journey and identify common friction points within the platform.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete an asynchronous screen recording task from your own computer. During the session, you will share your screen and narrate your process as you navigate through a standard Salesforce Marketing Cloud workflow. We will ask you to explain your decision-making, highlight any specific tools you rely on, and describe the outcome of the task. The entire activity is self-paced and requires a clear audio recording of your walkthrough.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for customer service professionals and support specialists who actively use Salesforce Marketing Cloud. We welcome customer success managers, service desk leads, and marketing support coordinators with hands-on platform experience. You should be comfortable demonstrating your workflows and articulating your process clearly on video.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Record a video walkthrough of a typical Salesforce Marketing Cloud task\n\n - Share your screen while navigating the platform interface\n\n - Narrate your process by explaining the steps you take and why\n\n - Highlight the features or tools you use most frequently during your workflow\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Current customer service or support professional\n\n - Hands-on experience using Salesforce Marketing Cloud\n\n - Comfortable recording your screen and providing clear audio commentary\n\n - Access to a reliable computer with a working microphone\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$70 per task\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/13a0726b-3698-4f78-82d1-ada921bc6dd6?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"65663465-4a23-419f-a421-ce903a7f1137","title":"Customer Service Professionals: ServiceNow Workflow Screen Recording","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-08T00:38:55.488+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/65663465-4a23-419f-a421-ce903a7f1137","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/65663465-4a23-419f-a421-ce903a7f1137/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the day-to-day software habits of customer support teams. Understanding how people actually navigate their primary tools helps us identify common friction points and system inefficiencies. We want to see real-world usage patterns to better comprehend the operational reality of service desks.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will capture a short, asynchronous screen recording of your desktop. During the recording, you will walk us through a common task or process you handle within the platform. You will narrate your actions out loud to explain the steps you take and the reasons behind them. Finally, you will submit the video for our team to review.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome customer service representatives, IT help desk agents, and support specialists. You must have hands-on experience using ServiceNow for ticketing, routing, or general service management. We are specifically looking for daily users who are comfortable explaining their digital workflows on camera.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Record an asynchronous video of your screen while navigating a common support task.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your specific workflow step by step.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Narrate your thought process and explain why you make certain system choices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Upload the finalized screen recording for our team to evaluate.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active customer service, support, or IT help desk professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience using ServiceNow in a professional setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with standard ticketing and resolution workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access to a computer capable of capturing screen and audio recordings</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$70 per task</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/dac80fb1-d178-4e70-a622-70a23c1f8d52?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the day-to-day software habits of customer support teams. Understanding how people actually navigate their primary tools helps us identify common friction points and system inefficiencies. We want to see real-world usage patterns to better comprehend the operational reality of service desks.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will capture a short, asynchronous screen recording of your desktop. During the recording, you will walk us through a common task or process you handle within the platform. You will narrate your actions out loud to explain the steps you take and the reasons behind them. Finally, you will submit the video for our team to review.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome customer service representatives, IT help desk agents, and support specialists. You must have hands-on experience using ServiceNow for ticketing, routing, or general service management. We are specifically looking for daily users who are comfortable explaining their digital workflows on camera.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Record an asynchronous video of your screen while navigating a common support task.\n\n - Walk us through your specific workflow step by step.\n\n - Narrate your thought process and explain why you make certain system choices.\n\n - Upload the finalized screen recording for our team to evaluate.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active customer service, support, or IT help desk professional\n\n - Hands-on experience using ServiceNow in a professional setting\n\n - Familiarity with standard ticketing and resolution workflows\n\n - Access to a computer capable of capturing screen and audio recordings\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$70 per task\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/dac80fb1-d178-4e70-a622-70a23c1f8d52?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"bab3e21c-7ee8-473f-9f55-bf067885dea0","title":"FP&A Consultants: Paid 1-Month Corporate Finance Project","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Brazil","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-08T02:46:10.520+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Brazil"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/bab3e21c-7ee8-473f-9f55-bf067885dea0","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/bab3e21c-7ee8-473f-9f55-bf067885dea0/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring a remote Corporate Finance Consultant for a dedicated one-month project. This engagement focuses on core financial planning and analysis workflows, supporting immediate strategic initiatives. The work feeds directly into ongoing financial modeling and corporate planning efforts.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will operate remotely for 40 hours per week over the course of a one-month engagement. The daily workflow involves building financial models, analyzing operational metrics, and structuring corporate finance data. You will share your screen during alignment calls and collaborate async on detailed financial deliverables. The project requires diving deep into existing financial frameworks and delivering actionable insights.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome Corporate Finance Consultants, FP&amp;A Analysts, and strategic finance professionals.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You should have 3-7 years of direct experience in corporate finance or financial planning and analysis. Candidates must be comfortable stepping into a high-impact, full-time remote engagement.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commit 40 hours per week to a remote, one-month consulting engagement</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and refine financial models to support strategic business decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analyze operational data and structure corporate finance metrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Communicate findings and progress through regular remote check-ins</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct background in corporate finance or FP&amp;A consulting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Between 3 and 7 years of relevant industry experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Capacity to commit to a 40-hour work week for a full month</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong proficiency with financial modeling and analysis tools</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$40 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/062a27bc-9247-4a34-a99d-be645318b592?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring a remote Corporate Finance Consultant for a dedicated one-month project. This engagement focuses on core financial planning and analysis workflows, supporting immediate strategic initiatives. The work feeds directly into ongoing financial modeling and corporate planning efforts.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will operate remotely for 40 hours per week over the course of a one-month engagement. The daily workflow involves building financial models, analyzing operational metrics, and structuring corporate finance data. You will share your screen during alignment calls and collaborate async on detailed financial deliverables. The project requires diving deep into existing financial frameworks and delivering actionable insights.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome Corporate Finance Consultants, FP&A Analysts, and strategic finance professionals.\n\nYou should have 3-7 years of direct experience in corporate finance or financial planning and analysis. Candidates must be comfortable stepping into a high-impact, full-time remote engagement.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Commit 40 hours per week to a remote, one-month consulting engagement\n\n - Build and refine financial models to support strategic business decisions\n\n - Analyze operational data and structure corporate finance metrics\n\n - Communicate findings and progress through regular remote check-ins\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Direct background in corporate finance or FP&A consulting\n\n - Between 3 and 7 years of relevant industry experience\n\n - Capacity to commit to a 40-hour work week for a full month\n\n - Strong proficiency with financial modeling and analysis tools\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$40 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/062a27bc-9247-4a34-a99d-be645318b592?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"b63c963e-27b6-4761-8531-2a541c64b603","title":"Multilingual Data Contributors: PDF Collection for AI Training","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-11T21:56:55.694+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/b63c963e-27b6-4761-8531-2a541c64b603","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/b63c963e-27b6-4761-8531-2a541c64b603/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on multilingual document sourcing to improve AI text recognition and generation. High-quality, legally usable PDFs in various languages are essential for training robust machine learning models. Your contributions will directly support the development of better language processing tools.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will work asynchronously to find and submit public, legally usable PDF documents in your designated language. During this process, you will verify that each document meets our quality and licensing requirements. You will upload the files through our secure platform and provide basic metadata for each submission. We will review your uploaded documents to ensure they match the project guidelines before approving the task.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are hiring fluent readers of Telugu, Odia, Gujarati, Malayalam, Japanese, and Korean who know how to source public documents online. Ideal candidates are detail-oriented individuals comfortable navigating digital archives, public records, or open-source repositories. We welcome data annotators, researchers, and general language contributors who understand basic copyright and licensing rules.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Source legally usable, public PDF documents in your designated language</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify that each document meets open-source or public domain licensing requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Upload the collected files to our research platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide basic descriptive information for each submitted document</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent reading comprehension in Telugu, Odia, Gujarati, Malayalam, Japanese, or Korean</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable searching for and downloading digital documents online</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Basic understanding of public domain or open-source licensing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Access to a reliable computer and internet connection for uploading files</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$150 per task</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/8dea52b6-365c-449f-9c7f-e4c456d53652?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on multilingual document sourcing to improve AI text recognition and generation. High-quality, legally usable PDFs in various languages are essential for training robust machine learning models. Your contributions will directly support the development of better language processing tools.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will work asynchronously to find and submit public, legally usable PDF documents in your designated language. During this process, you will verify that each document meets our quality and licensing requirements. You will upload the files through our secure platform and provide basic metadata for each submission. We will review your uploaded documents to ensure they match the project guidelines before approving the task.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are hiring fluent readers of Telugu, Odia, Gujarati, Malayalam, Japanese, and Korean who know how to source public documents online. Ideal candidates are detail-oriented individuals comfortable navigating digital archives, public records, or open-source repositories. We welcome data annotators, researchers, and general language contributors who understand basic copyright and licensing rules.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Source legally usable, public PDF documents in your designated language\n\n - Verify that each document meets open-source or public domain licensing requirements\n\n - Upload the collected files to our research platform\n\n - Provide basic descriptive information for each submitted document\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Fluent reading comprehension in Telugu, Odia, Gujarati, Malayalam, Japanese, or Korean\n\n - Comfortable searching for and downloading digital documents online\n\n - Basic understanding of public domain or open-source licensing\n\n - Access to a reliable computer and internet connection for uploading files\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$150 per task\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/8dea52b6-365c-449f-9c7f-e4c456d53652?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"a68ac752-95f4-41ca-8fc2-edc1c7025d00","title":"Business Professionals: 30-Minute Interview on Management Tools","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Ireland","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T20:20:32.256+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Ireland"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/a68ac752-95f4-41ca-8fc2-edc1c7025d00","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/a68ac752-95f4-41ca-8fc2-edc1c7025d00/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on how professionals interact with modern business management platforms. By understanding the pain points and successes you experience with these online tools, we can help improve digital services across various industries. Your insights will guide the next generation of business software design.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join a 30-minute remote interview via video call. During the session, we will ask you to discuss the specific online platforms you use to manage your daily business operations. You will be asked to walk us through a few recent examples of how you organized tasks, communicated with your team, or tracked progress. Finally, you will provide your candid feedback on what features work well and what needs improvement.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for active business professionals who rely on digital management tools to do their jobs. We welcome project managers, operations specialists, team leads, and small business owners. Ideal candidates should be comfortable discussing their software preferences and explaining their operational workflows in detail.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join a 30-minute remote video interview</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through the business management tools you use daily</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss specific challenges you face with your current online platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share suggestions for improving the digital services in your industry</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently employed in a business, operations, or management role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regular user of online business management platforms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable articulating your software workflows and preferences</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Able to join a remote video call from a quiet environment</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/cae0b6ec-60be-48c0-9ff5-4d8b727239ce?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on how professionals interact with modern business management platforms. By understanding the pain points and successes you experience with these online tools, we can help improve digital services across various industries. Your insights will guide the next generation of business software design.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will join a 30-minute remote interview via video call. During the session, we will ask you to discuss the specific online platforms you use to manage your daily business operations. You will be asked to walk us through a few recent examples of how you organized tasks, communicated with your team, or tracked progress. Finally, you will provide your candid feedback on what features work well and what needs improvement.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for active business professionals who rely on digital management tools to do their jobs. We welcome project managers, operations specialists, team leads, and small business owners. Ideal candidates should be comfortable discussing their software preferences and explaining their operational workflows in detail.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Join a 30-minute remote video interview\n\n - Walk us through the business management tools you use daily\n\n - Discuss specific challenges you face with your current online platforms\n\n - Share suggestions for improving the digital services in your industry\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Currently employed in a business, operations, or management role\n\n - Regular user of online business management platforms\n\n - Comfortable articulating your software workflows and preferences\n\n - Able to join a remote video call from a quiet environment\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/cae0b6ec-60be-48c0-9ff5-4d8b727239ce?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"273673d9-e951-43f5-a470-438828a7b4e7","title":"RL Environment Engineers: Building Tool Gyms For Knowledge Work","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-12T20:45:53.947+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/273673d9-e951-43f5-a470-438828a7b4e7","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/273673d9-e951-43f5-a470-438828a7b4e7/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring an RL environment engineer to help build tool-based environments, commonly known as tool gyms, for knowledge work applications. This paid engagement focuses on creating robust simulation frameworks where models can learn to interact with complex software tools. The resulting environments will directly support advanced reinforcement learning research and training pipelines.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will spend approximately 20 hours per week developing and testing new tool environments. This involves writing code to simulate various knowledge work tasks, ensuring realistic and stable agent interactions. You will also participate in remote video check-ins to discuss architecture decisions and troubleshoot implementation blockers. Throughout the project, you will iterate on environment designs based on model performance and technical feedback.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for specialized machine learning professionals with hands-on experience in reinforcement learning environments. We welcome RL engineers, AI researchers, simulation developers, and machine learning infrastructure specialists. Ideal candidates have previously built or maintained custom gyms and are comfortable committing to a part-time weekly schedule.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and implement tool-based environments for knowledge work simulations.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Write clean and modular code to support reinforcement learning training pipelines.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Troubleshoot and refine environment mechanics based on testing feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate asynchronously and participate in remote progress check-ins.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience as a machine learning or reinforcement learning engineer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on background building custom RL environments or tool gyms</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to commit to approximately 20 hours of work per week</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing technical architecture and implementation strategies</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/33cf6746-86a3-4b4f-b009-4b264c9e9c86?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring an RL environment engineer to help build tool-based environments, commonly known as tool gyms, for knowledge work applications. This paid engagement focuses on creating robust simulation frameworks where models can learn to interact with complex software tools. The resulting environments will directly support advanced reinforcement learning research and training pipelines.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will spend approximately 20 hours per week developing and testing new tool environments. This involves writing code to simulate various knowledge work tasks, ensuring realistic and stable agent interactions. You will also participate in remote video check-ins to discuss architecture decisions and troubleshoot implementation blockers. Throughout the project, you will iterate on environment designs based on model performance and technical feedback.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for specialized machine learning professionals with hands-on experience in reinforcement learning environments. We welcome RL engineers, AI researchers, simulation developers, and machine learning infrastructure specialists. Ideal candidates have previously built or maintained custom gyms and are comfortable committing to a part-time weekly schedule.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and implement tool-based environments for knowledge work simulations.\n\n - Write clean and modular code to support reinforcement learning training pipelines.\n\n - Troubleshoot and refine environment mechanics based on testing feedback.\n\n - Collaborate asynchronously and participate in remote progress check-ins.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience as a machine learning or reinforcement learning engineer\n\n - Hands-on background building custom RL environments or tool gyms\n\n - Ability to commit to approximately 20 hours of work per week\n\n - Comfortable discussing technical architecture and implementation strategies\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/33cf6746-86a3-4b4f-b009-4b264c9e9c86?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"17bc476e-05cb-48eb-961c-942e1f67e5df","title":"Health Plan Decision-Makers: Survey on PBM Contracting and Strategy","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T21:23:56.182+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/17bc476e-05cb-48eb-961c-942e1f67e5df","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/17bc476e-05cb-48eb-961c-942e1f67e5df/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the evolving landscape of Pharmacy Benefit Manager contracting. We want to understand the strategic drivers behind how payers evaluate, select, and manage these critical vendor relationships. Your input will help identify key trends in benefit management and payer priorities.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will complete a 25-minute remote survey covering your organization's approach to pharmacy benefits. The questions will walk through your vendor selection criteria, contract negotiation priorities, and ongoing performance management. You will evaluate different strategic scenarios and rank the factors most important to your decision-making process. The format is entirely asynchronous and can be completed at your convenience.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for senior leaders and decision-makers at health plans or payer organizations. You should have direct involvement in evaluating, selecting, or managing PBM contracts for your organization. We welcome pharmacy directors, contracting executives, network managers, and similar benefit strategy roles.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete a 25-minute asynchronous survey on your own schedule</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail your organization's criteria for selecting and evaluating pharmacy benefit partners</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rank the strategic priorities that drive your contracting decisions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide insights into current trends in pharmacy benefit management</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Current leadership or decision-making role at a health plan or payer organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience with Pharmacy Benefit Manager contracting and strategy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with the vendor selection and evaluation process</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$228 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/b28ece0b-4bed-4312-bb1f-e1b6ee35a2e4?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the evolving landscape of Pharmacy Benefit Manager contracting. We want to understand the strategic drivers behind how payers evaluate, select, and manage these critical vendor relationships. Your input will help identify key trends in benefit management and payer priorities.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete a 25-minute remote survey covering your organization's approach to pharmacy benefits. The questions will walk through your vendor selection criteria, contract negotiation priorities, and ongoing performance management. You will evaluate different strategic scenarios and rank the factors most important to your decision-making process. The format is entirely asynchronous and can be completed at your convenience.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for senior leaders and decision-makers at health plans or payer organizations. You should have direct involvement in evaluating, selecting, or managing PBM contracts for your organization. We welcome pharmacy directors, contracting executives, network managers, and similar benefit strategy roles.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Complete a 25-minute asynchronous survey on your own schedule\n\n - Detail your organization's criteria for selecting and evaluating pharmacy benefit partners\n\n - Rank the strategic priorities that drive your contracting decisions\n\n - Provide insights into current trends in pharmacy benefit management\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Current leadership or decision-making role at a health plan or payer organization\n\n - Direct experience with Pharmacy Benefit Manager contracting and strategy\n\n - Familiarity with the vendor selection and evaluation process\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$228 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/b28ece0b-4bed-4312-bb1f-e1b6ee35a2e4?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"e4c8d839-3ddd-4a92-b738-88b9ad7f5f47","title":"Benefits Decision-Makers: Feedback on Health and Pharmacy Plans","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T21:34:22.122+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/e4c8d839-3ddd-4a92-b738-88b9ad7f5f47","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/e4c8d839-3ddd-4a92-b738-88b9ad7f5f47/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the purchasing dynamics behind corporate health and pharmacy benefit plans. The goal is to map how large organizations structure their benefits packages to balance employee needs with cost controls. Your insights will help us understand the major pain points and decision drivers in the current health insurance market.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote video interview to discuss your company's benefits strategy. We will ask you to walk through a recent plan renewal or vendor selection process, highlighting what went well and what proved challenging. You will also review a set of hypothetical plan structures and provide feedback on their appeal. The conversation will focus heavily on how you evaluate pharmacy benefit managers and broader health networks.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for HR leaders and benefits directors at mid-market to enterprise companies. You should have direct involvement in selecting or managing health insurance and pharmacy benefit plans for your organization. We welcome VP of Total Rewards, Directors of Benefits, and Senior HR Business Partners who handle vendor negotiations.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe your current process for evaluating and renewing corporate health plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through how your organization approaches pharmacy benefits management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share feedback on what drives your final purchasing decisions during renewal cycles</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">React to different plan structures and discuss their feasibility for your workforce</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Senior HR, Total Rewards, or Benefits professional at a larger organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct decision-making authority or heavy influence over health insurance purchasing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with pharmacy benefit plan structures and vendor negotiations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing the financial and strategic trade-offs of benefit designs</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$175 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/c16a6e07-2dcf-4d0a-998f-50cbca981f0b?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the purchasing dynamics behind corporate health and pharmacy benefit plans. The goal is to map how large organizations structure their benefits packages to balance employee needs with cost controls. Your insights will help us understand the major pain points and decision drivers in the current health insurance market.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote video interview to discuss your company's benefits strategy. We will ask you to walk through a recent plan renewal or vendor selection process, highlighting what went well and what proved challenging. You will also review a set of hypothetical plan structures and provide feedback on their appeal. The conversation will focus heavily on how you evaluate pharmacy benefit managers and broader health networks.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for HR leaders and benefits directors at mid-market to enterprise companies. You should have direct involvement in selecting or managing health insurance and pharmacy benefit plans for your organization. We welcome VP of Total Rewards, Directors of Benefits, and Senior HR Business Partners who handle vendor negotiations.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Describe your current process for evaluating and renewing corporate health plans\n\n - Walk us through how your organization approaches pharmacy benefits management\n\n - Share feedback on what drives your final purchasing decisions during renewal cycles\n\n - React to different plan structures and discuss their feasibility for your workforce\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Senior HR, Total Rewards, or Benefits professional at a larger organization\n\n - Direct decision-making authority or heavy influence over health insurance purchasing\n\n - Familiarity with pharmacy benefit plan structures and vendor negotiations\n\n - Comfortable discussing the financial and strategic trade-offs of benefit designs\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$175 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/c16a6e07-2dcf-4d0a-998f-50cbca981f0b?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"32a80f0f-c78e-4e76-919d-06d72dfa8b94","title":"Benefits Decision Makers: Survey on Health Insurance Plans","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-13T21:43:59.665+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/32a80f0f-c78e-4e76-919d-06d72dfa8b94","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/32a80f0f-c78e-4e76-919d-06d72dfa8b94/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are running a paid study on the decision-making process behind corporate health insurance plans. Understanding how businesses evaluate different coverage options helps improve the benefits ecosystem for everyone. This research focuses on the pain points and priorities that drive yearly renewal choices.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will complete a remote, 25-minute asynchronous survey regarding your company's benefits administration. The survey asks you to walk through your recent experiences evaluating health insurance providers and managing employee enrollment. You will evaluate several common pain points and rank the features most critical to your organization. The entire process is self-paced and completed entirely online.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome HR professionals, benefits administrators, and business owners who actively manage corporate health insurance. You must have recent experience evaluating, selecting, or renewing health coverage for your organization. We welcome directors of HR, benefits managers, compensation specialists, and operations leads.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete a 25-minute asynchronous survey on your own schedule</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe the process your company uses to evaluate health insurance options</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify key challenges you face during the annual benefits renewal cycle</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rank the importance of various coverage features and provider tools</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional involved in HR, benefits, or business operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct involvement in selecting or managing corporate health insurance plans</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiar with the annual benefits renewal process</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable answering detailed questions about insurance administration workflows</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$120 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/cf2d50f4-a16b-4e48-b075-cf427ffb0c17?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe are running a paid study on the decision-making process behind corporate health insurance plans. Understanding how businesses evaluate different coverage options helps improve the benefits ecosystem for everyone. This research focuses on the pain points and priorities that drive yearly renewal choices.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete a remote, 25-minute asynchronous survey regarding your company's benefits administration. The survey asks you to walk through your recent experiences evaluating health insurance providers and managing employee enrollment. You will evaluate several common pain points and rank the features most critical to your organization. The entire process is self-paced and completed entirely online.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome HR professionals, benefits administrators, and business owners who actively manage corporate health insurance. You must have recent experience evaluating, selecting, or renewing health coverage for your organization. We welcome directors of HR, benefits managers, compensation specialists, and operations leads.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Complete a 25-minute asynchronous survey on your own schedule\n\n - Describe the process your company uses to evaluate health insurance options\n\n - Identify key challenges you face during the annual benefits renewal cycle\n\n - Rank the importance of various coverage features and provider tools\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional involved in HR, benefits, or business operations\n\n - Direct involvement in selecting or managing corporate health insurance plans\n\n - Familiar with the annual benefits renewal process\n\n - Comfortable answering detailed questions about insurance administration workflows\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$120 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/cf2d50f4-a16b-4e48-b075-cf427ffb0c17?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"af5a2497-c763-4b41-ad5a-c7ebf89c5b38","title":"Corporate Treasury Professionals: IFRS 9 Hedge Pack Review","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T21:40:46.586+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/af5a2497-c763-4b41-ad5a-c7ebf89c5b38","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/af5a2497-c763-4b41-ad5a-c7ebf89c5b38/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on corporate treasury compliance and technical hedge documentation. The goal is to evaluate the structure and clarity of a standard hedge pack under IFRS 9 guidelines. Your expertise will help us understand how financial professionals interact with complex FX cash flow hedging programs in practice.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote interview to review a technical corporate treasury hedge pack. During the session, we will ask you to evaluate specific sections of an FX cash flow hedging program for compliance with IFRS 9. You will share your screen to walk through the documentation and provide verbal feedback on its clarity and completeness. Finally, you will answer a series of technical questions regarding the hedge accounting methodology.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome corporate treasury professionals, hedge accounting specialists, and financial controllers with direct experience in FX cash flow hedging. Candidates should be comfortable reviewing technical documentation under IFRS 9 standards. If you manage corporate risk, oversee derivative accounting, or structure hedging programs, your background is a great fit for this study.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review a technical corporate treasury hedge pack for an FX cash flow hedging program</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the documentation for compliance with IFRS 9 guidelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your typical process for assessing hedge effectiveness</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide constructive feedback on the clarity and structure of the presented materials</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience in corporate treasury, hedge accounting, or financial control</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience working with FX cash flow hedging programs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong working knowledge of IFRS 9 hedge accounting requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable reviewing technical financial documentation on a remote video call</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/aa22be45-8c67-431a-94f8-fa7b1f4175fe?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on corporate treasury compliance and technical hedge documentation. The goal is to evaluate the structure and clarity of a standard hedge pack under IFRS 9 guidelines. Your expertise will help us understand how financial professionals interact with complex FX cash flow hedging programs in practice.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote interview to review a technical corporate treasury hedge pack. During the session, we will ask you to evaluate specific sections of an FX cash flow hedging program for compliance with IFRS 9. You will share your screen to walk through the documentation and provide verbal feedback on its clarity and completeness. Finally, you will answer a series of technical questions regarding the hedge accounting methodology.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome corporate treasury professionals, hedge accounting specialists, and financial controllers with direct experience in FX cash flow hedging. Candidates should be comfortable reviewing technical documentation under IFRS 9 standards. If you manage corporate risk, oversee derivative accounting, or structure hedging programs, your background is a great fit for this study.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Review a technical corporate treasury hedge pack for an FX cash flow hedging program\n\n - Evaluate the documentation for compliance with IFRS 9 guidelines\n\n - Walk us through your typical process for assessing hedge effectiveness\n\n - Provide constructive feedback on the clarity and structure of the presented materials\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience in corporate treasury, hedge accounting, or financial control\n\n - Direct experience working with FX cash flow hedging programs\n\n - Strong working knowledge of IFRS 9 hedge accounting requirements\n\n - Comfortable reviewing technical financial documentation on a remote video call\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/aa22be45-8c67-431a-94f8-fa7b1f4175fe?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"557b318b-1bdc-400a-8057-5534545e4c6c","title":"Logistics Managers: Parcel Shipping Contracts And Carrier Allocation","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T20:54:39.334+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/557b318b-1bdc-400a-8057-5534545e4c6c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/557b318b-1bdc-400a-8057-5534545e4c6c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the strategies organizations use to negotiate parcel shipping agreements. Carrier allocation and contract terms have a massive impact on supply chain efficiency, and we want to understand the decision-making process behind these choices. Your insights will help us map the current landscape of logistics partnerships.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will join a remote video interview to walk us through your approach to managing shipping logistics. We will ask you to detail how your organization negotiates contracts and allocates package volume among various carriers. You will discuss the primary factors that influence your carrier selection, including pricing, reliability, and service level agreements. The conversation will focus entirely on your professional methodology and past experiences managing these operational challenges.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome logistics managers, supply chain directors, and procurement specialists who actively oversee shipping operations. You should have direct experience negotiating contracts with major parcel carriers and managing outbound volume distribution. Candidates with a background in e-commerce fulfillment, enterprise shipping, or global logistics are highly encouraged to apply.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe how your organization negotiates parcel shipping contracts</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explain your methodology for allocating package volume across different carriers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through the metrics you use to evaluate carrier performance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share recent experiences adapting to changing shipping costs or capacity constraints</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active role in supply chain, logistics, or procurement management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct involvement in negotiating contracts with parcel shipping carriers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with enterprise package volume allocation</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing operational strategies in a remote interview setting</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$133 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/fe146a86-ec10-48f3-b807-883cf731cc44?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2