contracts\n\n - Explain your methodology for allocating package volume across different carriers\n\n - Walk us through the metrics you use to evaluate carrier performance\n\n - Share recent experiences adapting to changing shipping costs or capacity constraints\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active role in supply chain, logistics, or procurement management\n\n - Direct involvement in negotiating contracts with parcel shipping carriers\n\n - Familiarity with enterprise package volume allocation\n\n - Comfortable discussing operational strategies in a remote interview setting\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$133 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/fe146a86-ec10-48f3-b807-883cf731cc44?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"38e5a0d5-2a8d-43ef-881d-1583bbc765b1","title":"Technical Accounting And FP&A Experts: AI Training Scenarios","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T00:28:31.880+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/38e5a0d5-2a8d-43ef-881d-1583bbc765b1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/38e5a0d5-2a8d-43ef-881d-1583bbc765b1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring technical accounting and FP&amp;A experts to help build reinforcement learning environments for AI systems. This work focuses on creating complex financial scenarios, defining edge cases, and establishing evaluation rubrics. Your contributions will directly improve how artificial intelligence handles sophisticated financial and accounting tasks.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote session to design and author technical accounting scenarios. During the task, you will document complex FP&amp;A edge cases and build corresponding evaluation rubrics. You will also peer-review scenarios created by other professionals to ensure accuracy and depth. The entire process takes place through a remote platform where you can submit and review written financial logic.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for experienced professionals in technical accounting, financial planning, and analysis. We welcome CPAs, FP&amp;A directors, controllers, and senior financial analysts with deep technical expertise. Candidates should be highly comfortable navigating complex financial edge cases and structuring logical evaluation criteria.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and author technical accounting scenarios and edge cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build evaluation rubrics for financial planning and analysis tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Peer-review financial scenarios created by other experts for accuracy</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Structure complex financial logic for AI reinforcement learning environments</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience in technical accounting or FP&amp;A</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong understanding of complex financial edge cases</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with creating structured evaluation criteria or rubrics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to clearly document and explain advanced accounting principles</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/ca2155de-753f-47ba-b04d-c041bf58aeac?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring technical accounting and FP&A experts to help build reinforcement learning environments for AI systems. This work focuses on creating complex financial scenarios, defining edge cases, and establishing evaluation rubrics. Your contributions will directly improve how artificial intelligence handles sophisticated financial and accounting tasks.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote session to design and author technical accounting scenarios. During the task, you will document complex FP&A edge cases and build corresponding evaluation rubrics. You will also peer-review scenarios created by other professionals to ensure accuracy and depth. The entire process takes place through a remote platform where you can submit and review written financial logic.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for experienced professionals in technical accounting, financial planning, and analysis. We welcome CPAs, FP&A directors, controllers, and senior financial analysts with deep technical expertise. Candidates should be highly comfortable navigating complex financial edge cases and structuring logical evaluation criteria.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and author technical accounting scenarios and edge cases\n\n - Build evaluation rubrics for financial planning and analysis tasks\n\n - Peer-review financial scenarios created by other experts for accuracy\n\n - Structure complex financial logic for AI reinforcement learning environments\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience in technical accounting or FP&A\n\n - Strong understanding of complex financial edge cases\n\n - Familiarity with creating structured evaluation criteria or rubrics\n\n - Ability to clearly document and explain advanced accounting principles\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/ca2155de-753f-47ba-b04d-c041bf58aeac?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"5f0027e3-8556-4c7e-91d3-c61f1b74a152","title":"User Researchers: Feedback On New Analysis Tools","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-20T18:37:45.860+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/5f0027e3-8556-4c7e-91d3-c61f1b74a152","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/5f0027e3-8556-4c7e-91d3-c61f1b74a152/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the next generation of user research tools. We are currently designing a new approach for analyzing and synthesizing qualitative research findings. Your feedback will directly influence how we build these analysis features to better serve product teams.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">During a 20-minute remote session, an AI moderator will guide you through our latest product concepts. You will review early design mockups and share your honest reactions to the proposed workflows. We will ask you to compare these new concepts against your current methods for analyzing research data. The entire conversation takes place via an interactive voice and screen-sharing setup.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This study is tailored for professionals who actively analyze user research findings in their day-to-day work. We welcome UX researchers, product managers, product designers, and consumer insights specialists. Ideal candidates have experience synthesizing qualitative data and are comfortable critiquing early-stage software concepts.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review early design concepts for a new research analysis tool</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share your honest and unfiltered reactions with an AI moderator</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compare the proposed features to your current data synthesis workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide constructive feedback on how the interface could better serve your needs</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active role in user research, product management, or product design</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience analyzing and synthesizing qualitative research findings</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable participating in an AI-moderated interview</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to review and critique early software concepts</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$88 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"http://localhost:3000/interview/start/r/3b2e15d3-d6af-470b-aa54-79c46654049a?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the next generation of user research tools. We are currently designing a new approach for analyzing and synthesizing qualitative research findings. Your feedback will directly influence how we build these analysis features to better serve product teams.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nDuring a 20-minute remote session, an AI moderator will guide you through our latest product concepts. You will review early design mockups and share your honest reactions to the proposed workflows. We will ask you to compare these new concepts against your current methods for analyzing research data. The entire conversation takes place via an interactive voice and screen-sharing setup.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nThis study is tailored for professionals who actively analyze user research findings in their day-to-day work. We welcome UX researchers, product managers, product designers, and consumer insights specialists. Ideal candidates have experience synthesizing qualitative data and are comfortable critiquing early-stage software concepts.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Review early design concepts for a new research analysis tool\n\n - Share your honest and unfiltered reactions with an AI moderator\n\n - Compare the proposed features to your current data synthesis workflows\n\n - Provide constructive feedback on how the interface could better serve your needs\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active role in user research, product management, or product design\n\n - Hands-on experience analyzing and synthesizing qualitative research findings\n\n - Comfortable participating in an AI-moderated interview\n\n - Willingness to review and critique early software concepts\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$88 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now http://localhost:3000/interview/start/r/3b2e15d3-d6af-470b-aa54-79c46654049a?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"dcaa84c2-755a-4ec0-8ef2-259142779027","title":"Equity Research Analysts: Evaluation of Coverage Draft Notes","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T22:05:41.586+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/dcaa84c2-755a-4ec0-8ef2-259142779027","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/dcaa84c2-755a-4ec0-8ef2-259142779027/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring equity research professionals to evaluate initiation of coverage draft notes for a paid study. The goal of this research is to ensure financial forecasts, valuation methodologies, and accounting practices meet high analytical standards. Your insights will help us refine our financial modeling evaluation processes and identify common accounting inconsistencies in early-stage coverage reports.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">During this remote session, you will be presented with an initiation of coverage draft note for a specific asset or company. You will walk us through your process for reviewing the attached valuation methodologies and financial forecasts. We will ask you to actively identify any analytical errors, accounting inconsistencies, or gaps in the provided financial models. Finally, you will provide structural feedback on how the draft note compares to standard institutional research reports.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for seasoned equity research analysts, investment analysts, and financial modeling experts who regularly produce or review coverage notes. You should have strong practical experience with valuation methodologies and deep knowledge of accounting principles. We welcome sell-side equity analysts, buy-side investment analysts, and portfolio managers who are comfortable tearing down complex financial forecasts.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review an initiation of coverage draft note and its accompanying financial models.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the accuracy and logic of the proposed valuation methodologies.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify analytical gaps, accounting inconsistencies, or aggressive forecasting assumptions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your thought process for validating institutional financial research.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience as an equity research analyst, investment analyst, or similar financial role.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in reviewing or authoring initiation of coverage notes.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep understanding of valuation methodologies and financial forecasting.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable identifying and explaining accounting inconsistencies in complex models.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/66b6a26b-4478-4f19-beeb-59b7242a158f?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring equity research professionals to evaluate initiation of coverage draft notes for a paid study. The goal of this research is to ensure financial forecasts, valuation methodologies, and accounting practices meet high analytical standards. Your insights will help us refine our financial modeling evaluation processes and identify common accounting inconsistencies in early-stage coverage reports.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nDuring this remote session, you will be presented with an initiation of coverage draft note for a specific asset or company. You will walk us through your process for reviewing the attached valuation methodologies and financial forecasts. We will ask you to actively identify any analytical errors, accounting inconsistencies, or gaps in the provided financial models. Finally, you will provide structural feedback on how the draft note compares to standard institutional research reports.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for seasoned equity research analysts, investment analysts, and financial modeling experts who regularly produce or review coverage notes. You should have strong practical experience with valuation methodologies and deep knowledge of accounting principles. We welcome sell-side equity analysts, buy-side investment analysts, and portfolio managers who are comfortable tearing down complex financial forecasts.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Review an initiation of coverage draft note and its accompanying financial models.\n\n - Evaluate the accuracy and logic of the proposed valuation methodologies.\n\n - Identify analytical gaps, accounting inconsistencies, or aggressive forecasting assumptions.\n\n - Walk us through your thought process for validating institutional financial research.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience as an equity research analyst, investment analyst, or similar financial role.\n\n - Strong background in reviewing or authoring initiation of coverage notes.\n\n - Deep understanding of valuation methodologies and financial forecasting.\n\n - Comfortable identifying and explaining accounting inconsistencies in complex models.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/66b6a26b-4478-4f19-beeb-59b7242a158f?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"33565e5b-13ac-444c-bc8d-d53f9ee5c775","title":"Corporate Finance Professionals: Flexible Financial Modeling Project","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-19T00:11:40.729+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/33565e5b-13ac-444c-bc8d-d53f9ee5c775","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/33565e5b-13ac-444c-bc8d-d53f9ee5c775/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring corporate finance and FP&amp;A experts for an extended paid project focused on financial modeling. This initiative evaluates how professionals approach complex financial analysis and strategic forecasting. The insights will help baseline advanced modeling workflows and improve financial tooling.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote, flexible project requiring around 20 hours per week. During the engagement, you will build and review financial models, analyze corporate data sets, and document your strategic decision-making process. You will share your screen during key analytical steps to walk us through your methodology. The work is mostly asynchronous, allowing you to complete tasks on your own schedule while meeting weekly milestones.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for experienced finance practitioners based in the US with strong modeling backgrounds. We welcome corporate finance professionals, FP&amp;A analysts, and strategic finance experts. A deep understanding of financial forecasting and data analysis is essential for this project.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build and evaluate complex financial models based on provided corporate data.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Document your analytical process and strategic forecasting decisions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your methodology using asynchronous screen sharing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Commit around 20 hours per week to complete assigned modeling tasks.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active professional in corporate finance, FP&amp;A, or strategic finance</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extensive hands-on experience with financial modeling and forecasting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable explaining complex financial analyses clearly</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in the United States</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/153186da-6f55-48ab-b764-de2bfab69ae9?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring corporate finance and FP&A experts for an extended paid project focused on financial modeling. This initiative evaluates how professionals approach complex financial analysis and strategic forecasting. The insights will help baseline advanced modeling workflows and improve financial tooling.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote, flexible project requiring around 20 hours per week. During the engagement, you will build and review financial models, analyze corporate data sets, and document your strategic decision-making process. You will share your screen during key analytical steps to walk us through your methodology. The work is mostly asynchronous, allowing you to complete tasks on your own schedule while meeting weekly milestones.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for experienced finance practitioners based in the US with strong modeling backgrounds. We welcome corporate finance professionals, FP&A analysts, and strategic finance experts. A deep understanding of financial forecasting and data analysis is essential for this project.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Build and evaluate complex financial models based on provided corporate data.\n\n - Document your analytical process and strategic forecasting decisions.\n\n - Walk us through your methodology using asynchronous screen sharing.\n\n - Commit around 20 hours per week to complete assigned modeling tasks.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active professional in corporate finance, FP&A, or strategic finance\n\n - Extensive hands-on experience with financial modeling and forecasting\n\n - Comfortable explaining complex financial analyses clearly\n\n - Based in the United States\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/153186da-6f55-48ab-b764-de2bfab69ae9?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"ec9e64bc-6be8-4b94-9265-73be5dcca864","title":"Software Engineers (Genomics): Architecting Computational Pipelines","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-17T22:46:12.668+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/ec9e64bc-6be8-4b94-9265-73be5dcca864","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/ec9e64bc-6be8-4b94-9265-73be5dcca864/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring software engineers to discuss the architecture of scalable computational pipelines for genomic data. Building these environments from scratch requires a unique intersection of domain knowledge and engineering rigor. Your feedback will inform how robust bioinformatics infrastructure is designed and deployed.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote, AI-moderated interview focused on your engineering workflows. During the session, you will walk us through how you design and build scalable environments from the ground up. We will ask you to detail the specific challenges of handling bioinformatics data and the technical tradeoffs you make. The conversation will flow through your recent projects, architectural decisions, and deployment strategies.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome backend software engineers, bioinformatics scientists, genomics data engineers, and computational biologists with strong architectural experience. You should have a proven track record of building scalable data pipelines from scratch. Ideal candidates will be highly comfortable discussing both the biological domain constraints and the underlying software engineering principles.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your process for architecting computational pipelines from scratch</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Explain how you handle the unique scale and complexity of genomic data</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss the technical tradeoffs involved in building bioinformatics environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail your deployment strategies and infrastructure choices</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience as a software engineer or computational data engineer</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Deep domain expertise in genomics or bioinformatics</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on background in building scalable computational environments from the ground up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing technical architectural decisions</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/effc758f-2df0-44d9-96a1-d1a9be3b2446?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring software engineers to discuss the architecture of scalable computational pipelines for genomic data. Building these environments from scratch requires a unique intersection of domain knowledge and engineering rigor. Your feedback will inform how robust bioinformatics infrastructure is designed and deployed.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote, AI-moderated interview focused on your engineering workflows. During the session, you will walk us through how you design and build scalable environments from the ground up. We will ask you to detail the specific challenges of handling bioinformatics data and the technical tradeoffs you make. The conversation will flow through your recent projects, architectural decisions, and deployment strategies.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome backend software engineers, bioinformatics scientists, genomics data engineers, and computational biologists with strong architectural experience. You should have a proven track record of building scalable data pipelines from scratch. Ideal candidates will be highly comfortable discussing both the biological domain constraints and the underlying software engineering principles.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Walk us through your process for architecting computational pipelines from scratch\n\n - Explain how you handle the unique scale and complexity of genomic data\n\n - Discuss the technical tradeoffs involved in building bioinformatics environments\n\n - Detail your deployment strategies and infrastructure choices\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience as a software engineer or computational data engineer\n\n - Deep domain expertise in genomics or bioinformatics\n\n - Hands-on background in building scalable computational environments from the ground up\n\n - Comfortable discussing technical architectural decisions\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/effc758f-2df0-44d9-96a1-d1a9be3b2446?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"27738f3d-9d31-467e-bed3-477ddf238806","title":"Outpatient Physicians and GPs: Paid Interview on Clinical Workflows","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-21T19:36:58.332+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/27738f3d-9d31-467e-bed3-477ddf238806","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/27738f3d-9d31-467e-bed3-477ddf238806/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on clinical workflows within outpatient clinics and private practices. This research focuses on understanding the daily operational challenges and administrative tasks that doctors handle. Our goal is to gather firsthand insights that will help shape the next generation of medical practice tools.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">During this remote interview, you will speak directly with our team about your typical clinical day. You will be asked to walk through how you manage patient intake, chart reviews, and general administrative duties. We will also ask you to react to a few conceptual ideas for streamlining clinic operations. The conversation will focus heavily on your honest experiences and pain points in outpatient care.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for practicing physicians and general practitioners who currently work in an outpatient clinic or private practice. We welcome family medicine doctors, internal medicine specialists, and other general practitioners actively seeing patients. Candidates must be comfortable discussing their clinical routines and practice management software.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your typical daily routine in an outpatient setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss the administrative and clinical challenges you face in private practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">React to conceptual ideas aimed at improving clinical workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share honest feedback on the tools you use for patient management</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Practicing physician or general practitioner</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently working in an outpatient clinic or private practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing day-to-day clinical operations and administrative tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Based in the US, Canada, UK, Australia, or New Zealand</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$100 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/b43cff66-e6da-4003-80a2-2941c8c18465?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on clinical workflows within outpatient clinics and private practices. This research focuses on understanding the daily operational challenges and administrative tasks that doctors handle. Our goal is to gather firsthand insights that will help shape the next generation of medical practice tools.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nDuring this remote interview, you will speak directly with our team about your typical clinical day. You will be asked to walk through how you manage patient intake, chart reviews, and general administrative duties. We will also ask you to react to a few conceptual ideas for streamlining clinic operations. The conversation will focus heavily on your honest experiences and pain points in outpatient care.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for practicing physicians and general practitioners who currently work in an outpatient clinic or private practice. We welcome family medicine doctors, internal medicine specialists, and other general practitioners actively seeing patients. Candidates must be comfortable discussing their clinical routines and practice management software.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Walk us through your typical daily routine in an outpatient setting\n\n - Discuss the administrative and clinical challenges you face in private practice\n\n - React to conceptual ideas aimed at improving clinical workflows\n\n - Share honest feedback on the tools you use for patient management\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Practicing physician or general practitioner\n\n - Currently working in an outpatient clinic or private practice\n\n - Comfortable discussing day-to-day clinical operations and administrative tasks\n\n - Based in the US, Canada, UK, Australia, or New Zealand\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$100 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/b43cff66-e6da-4003-80a2-2941c8c18465?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"4ae36712-0817-4ff5-8aa9-3cd96bccd891","title":"Video Review Tool Users: Feedback on Menu Organization","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T17:14:55.926+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/4ae36712-0817-4ff5-8aa9-3cd96bccd891","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/4ae36712-0817-4ff5-8aa9-3cd96bccd891/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the usability of online tools used to review, share, and manage video files. Our team is specifically working on improving how a common menu is organized within these interfaces. Your input will help us build a more intuitive navigation experience for daily users.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will complete a remote online activity lasting 15-20 minutes. During this session, you will review early designs of a menu structure and provide feedback on how items are grouped. You will be asked to sort specific features into the categories that make the most sense to your workflow. We will also ask a few questions about your typical experience managing media files.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome professionals and creators who regularly use online tools to review, share, and manage video or other media files. This includes video editors, content managers, producers, and active media collaborators. If you rely on digital review platforms for your daily workflow, we want to hear from you.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete a 15-20 minute online usability activity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate how a common menu is organized in a media management tool</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Categorize features and tools based on your typical workflow needs</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share brief feedback on your experience reviewing and sharing video files</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Regular user of an online tool to review, share, or manage media files</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiar with common video collaboration and editing workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable providing clear feedback on user interfaces and menu structures</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$20 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/5b1cd04b-108a-4101-8c33-8e5bf1f2fd56?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the usability of online tools used to review, share, and manage video files. Our team is specifically working on improving how a common menu is organized within these interfaces. Your input will help us build a more intuitive navigation experience for daily users.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete a remote online activity lasting 15-20 minutes. During this session, you will review early designs of a menu structure and provide feedback on how items are grouped. You will be asked to sort specific features into the categories that make the most sense to your workflow. We will also ask a few questions about your typical experience managing media files.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome professionals and creators who regularly use online tools to review, share, and manage video or other media files. This includes video editors, content managers, producers, and active media collaborators. If you rely on digital review platforms for your daily workflow, we want to hear from you.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Complete a 15-20 minute online usability activity\n\n - Evaluate how a common menu is organized in a media management tool\n\n - Categorize features and tools based on your typical workflow needs\n\n - Share brief feedback on your experience reviewing and sharing video files\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Regular user of an online tool to review, share, or manage media files\n\n - Familiar with common video collaboration and editing workflows\n\n - Comfortable providing clear feedback on user interfaces and menu structures\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$20 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/5b1cd04b-108a-4101-8c33-8e5bf1f2fd56?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"d062513a-b76d-4b4f-89b8-021f713ac750","title":"Technical Individual Contributors: Feedback on Online Learning Prototypes","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T21:05:45.005+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/d062513a-b76d-4b4f-89b8-021f713ac750","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/d062513a-b76d-4b4f-89b8-021f713ac750/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the future of online learning platforms tailored for technical skill development. Evaluating early concepts helps us understand what features actually support professional growth in complex roles. Your feedback will directly influence how these educational tools are structured and designed.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">During a 40-minute remote video call, you will discuss your past experiences with online learning and technical upskilling. We will then ask you to share your screen and interact with early prototype concepts. You will provide live, candid feedback on the interface, content structure, and overall usability. The conversation will focus on identifying what works well and what could be improved in the learning experience.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome individual contributors currently working in engineering, IT, data, or product management roles. You should have an interest in professional development and prior experience using online learning platforms to build technical skills. Ideal candidates are comfortable articulating their thought process while navigating new software interfaces.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss your current approach to technical skill development and online education.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and interact with early-stage prototype concepts for a learning platform.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide live verbal feedback on usability, features, and overall design choices.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through what you find valuable or frustrating in the concepts shown.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Current individual contributor in a technical field (engineering, IT, data, or product)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with using online platforms for professional development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable sharing your screen and thinking aloud during a remote video session</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$135 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/501ad4a7-0181-4582-b4b3-33a21febd2e7?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the future of online learning platforms tailored for technical skill development. Evaluating early concepts helps us understand what features actually support professional growth in complex roles. Your feedback will directly influence how these educational tools are structured and designed.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nDuring a 40-minute remote video call, you will discuss your past experiences with online learning and technical upskilling. We will then ask you to share your screen and interact with early prototype concepts. You will provide live, candid feedback on the interface, content structure, and overall usability. The conversation will focus on identifying what works well and what could be improved in the learning experience.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome individual contributors currently working in engineering, IT, data, or product management roles. You should have an interest in professional development and prior experience using online learning platforms to build technical skills. Ideal candidates are comfortable articulating their thought process while navigating new software interfaces.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Discuss your current approach to technical skill development and online education.\n\n - Review and interact with early-stage prototype concepts for a learning platform.\n\n - Provide live verbal feedback on usability, features, and overall design choices.\n\n - Walk us through what you find valuable or frustrating in the concepts shown.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Current individual contributor in a technical field (engineering, IT, data, or product)\n\n - Familiarity with using online platforms for professional development\n\n - Comfortable sharing your screen and thinking aloud during a remote video session\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$135 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/501ad4a7-0181-4582-b4b3-33a21febd2e7?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"20fbfae1-1e63-430d-a3af-2fb2a6952596","title":"US Healthcare Professionals: Interview On Medication Selection","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T21:51:54.083+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/20fbfae1-1e63-430d-a3af-2fb2a6952596","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/20fbfae1-1e63-430d-a3af-2fb2a6952596/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on how clinical providers approach medication selection and therapeutic recommendations. Understanding the factors that drive prescribing choices helps us map the real-world workflow of modern patient care. This research aims to identify the clinical, logistical, and patient-specific variables that influence treatment paths.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">During a remote video session, you will participate in a moderated conversation about your clinical workflow. We will ask you to walk through recent examples of how you evaluate different medication options for your patients. You will review a series of hypothetical patient scenarios and explain your reasoning for recommending specific treatments. Finally, you will provide feedback on the primary challenges you face when ordering or prescribing therapies.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for US-based physicians and healthcare professionals with active prescribing authority. We welcome attendings, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, and clinical specialists who regularly make medication recommendations. Ideal candidates will have hands-on experience navigating treatment selection and ordering therapies within the past year.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your current workflow for evaluating and selecting patient medications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss the primary factors that influence your clinical recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review hypothetical patient scenarios and explain your treatment choices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Share insights on the challenges associated with prescribing and ordering therapies</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active US-based physician or healthcare professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Current authority or influence over medication selection and prescribing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Recent clinical experience ordering therapies or making treatment recommendations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing patient care workflows in a remote video setting</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$175 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/13561df4-01e2-4d12-8f7d-cae3dc389856?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on how clinical providers approach medication selection and therapeutic recommendations. Understanding the factors that drive prescribing choices helps us map the real-world workflow of modern patient care. This research aims to identify the clinical, logistical, and patient-specific variables that influence treatment paths.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nDuring a remote video session, you will participate in a moderated conversation about your clinical workflow. We will ask you to walk through recent examples of how you evaluate different medication options for your patients. You will review a series of hypothetical patient scenarios and explain your reasoning for recommending specific treatments. Finally, you will provide feedback on the primary challenges you face when ordering or prescribing therapies.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for US-based physicians and healthcare professionals with active prescribing authority. We welcome attendings, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, and clinical specialists who regularly make medication recommendations. Ideal candidates will have hands-on experience navigating treatment selection and ordering therapies within the past year.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Walk us through your current workflow for evaluating and selecting patient medications\n\n - Discuss the primary factors that influence your clinical recommendations\n\n - Review hypothetical patient scenarios and explain your treatment choices\n\n - Share insights on the challenges associated with prescribing and ordering therapies\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active US-based physician or healthcare professional\n\n - Current authority or influence over medication selection and prescribing\n\n - Recent clinical experience ordering therapies or making treatment recommendations\n\n - Comfortable discussing patient care workflows in a remote video setting\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$175 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/13561df4-01e2-4d12-8f7d-cae3dc389856?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"6ad7a9c1-2108-418a-b601-0f41e928cc0c","title":"Healthcare Administrators: Payer Interaction Workflow Survey","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T22:05:34.742+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/6ad7a9c1-2108-418a-b601-0f41e928cc0c","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/6ad7a9c1-2108-418a-b601-0f41e928cc0c/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the day-to-day realities of payer interactions in healthcare practices. Our goal is to understand the administrative friction points involved in credentialing, contracting, and prior authorizations. Your input will help us evaluate current workflow challenges and identify areas for operational improvement.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will complete an asynchronous, remote survey detailing your practice's administrative workflows. The survey will ask you to walk through your standard processes for handling claims and interacting with payers. You will react to specific workflow scenarios and estimate the time spent on various administrative tasks. The entire process is conducted online and can be completed at your convenience.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome practice managers, billing specialists, and healthcare administrators who handle payer interactions. You should have direct experience managing contracting, credentialing, or claims for a provider organization. Professionals working in small to mid-sized practices are highly encouraged to apply.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete a remote survey regarding your payer interaction workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail your daily processes for credentialing, prior authorizations, and claims management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe the administrative hurdles you face when contracting with payers</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate the efficiency of your current practice management strategies</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Healthcare professional involved in practice administration or billing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with payer interactions and contracting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with prior authorization and claims workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently employed at a healthcare provider organization</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$123 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/ccc5f86f-e28a-404f-b416-8e68fd3c4d7a?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the day-to-day realities of payer interactions in healthcare practices. Our goal is to understand the administrative friction points involved in credentialing, contracting, and prior authorizations. Your input will help us evaluate current workflow challenges and identify areas for operational improvement.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete an asynchronous, remote survey detailing your practice's administrative workflows. The survey will ask you to walk through your standard processes for handling claims and interacting with payers. You will react to specific workflow scenarios and estimate the time spent on various administrative tasks. The entire process is conducted online and can be completed at your convenience.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome practice managers, billing specialists, and healthcare administrators who handle payer interactions. You should have direct experience managing contracting, credentialing, or claims for a provider organization. Professionals working in small to mid-sized practices are highly encouraged to apply.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Complete a remote survey regarding your payer interaction workflows\n\n - Detail your daily processes for credentialing, prior authorizations, and claims management\n\n - Describe the administrative hurdles you face when contracting with payers\n\n - Evaluate the efficiency of your current practice management strategies\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Healthcare professional involved in practice administration or billing\n\n - Hands-on experience with payer interactions and contracting\n\n - Familiarity with prior authorization and claims workflows\n\n - Currently employed at a healthcare provider organization\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$123 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/ccc5f86f-e28a-404f-b416-8e68fd3c4d7a?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"80d97fb9-cbfa-4147-a66b-8a974a03738f","title":"Healthcare Admin Staff: Survey on Payer Interactions","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-27T22:37:31.529+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/80d97fb9-cbfa-4147-a66b-8a974a03738f","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/80d97fb9-cbfa-4147-a66b-8a974a03738f/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the administrative workflows that keep healthcare provider organizations running. We want to understand the friction points in daily payer interactions, from prior authorizations to revenue cycle management. Your input will help identify areas where administrative tools can be streamlined.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will complete an asynchronous remote survey detailing your day-to-day administrative tasks. We will ask you to walk through how you handle billing, credentialing, and prior authorizations within your organization. You will also react to different scenarios involving payer interactions and describe any current workflow challenges you face. The entire process is conducted online and allows you to share your experiences directly.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome healthcare administrative professionals who work directly for provider organizations. We are specifically looking for billing specialists, credentialing coordinators, revenue cycle managers, and prior authorization staff. If you handle daily payer interactions and backend administrative workflows, this study is a great fit.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail your daily workflows involving payer interactions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe how you handle billing, credentialing, or prior authorization tasks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify common challenges and friction points in your revenue cycle management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate current administrative workflows used in your organization</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently employed at a healthcare provider organization</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct involvement in payer interactions and administrative workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with billing, credentialing, or prior authorization processes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable providing detailed written feedback in an online survey</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$105 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/25405ad4-d5c9-466e-975f-ff6853779e73?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the administrative workflows that keep healthcare provider organizations running. We want to understand the friction points in daily payer interactions, from prior authorizations to revenue cycle management. Your input will help identify areas where administrative tools can be streamlined.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete an asynchronous remote survey detailing your day-to-day administrative tasks. We will ask you to walk through how you handle billing, credentialing, and prior authorizations within your organization. You will also react to different scenarios involving payer interactions and describe any current workflow challenges you face. The entire process is conducted online and allows you to share your experiences directly.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome healthcare administrative professionals who work directly for provider organizations. We are specifically looking for billing specialists, credentialing coordinators, revenue cycle managers, and prior authorization staff. If you handle daily payer interactions and backend administrative workflows, this study is a great fit.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Detail your daily workflows involving payer interactions\n\n - Describe how you handle billing, credentialing, or prior authorization tasks\n\n - Identify common challenges and friction points in your revenue cycle management\n\n - Evaluate current administrative workflows used in your organization\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Currently employed at a healthcare provider organization\n\n - Direct involvement in payer interactions and administrative workflows\n\n - Familiarity with billing, credentialing, or prior authorization processes\n\n - Comfortable providing detailed written feedback in an online survey\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$105 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/25405ad4-d5c9-466e-975f-ff6853779e73?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"da97749c-74b5-4075-9935-9034c5c2d6da","title":"Biology PhDs: Paid Expert Contributions in Genetics and Biochemistry","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-01T17:59:33.128+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/da97749c-74b5-4075-9935-9034c5c2d6da","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/da97749c-74b5-4075-9935-9034c5c2d6da/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring biology PhDs to provide ongoing technical expertise in genetics, protein engineering, and biochemistry. This long-term research effort aims to evaluate complex biological data and map out emerging scientific trends. Your domain knowledge will directly support the evaluation of advanced computational biology models and literature reviews.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in remote tasks and occasional video interviews to evaluate technical biological concepts. Expect to review academic literature, analyze protein structures, or assess genetic data sets based on specific prompts. You will provide detailed written feedback and walk us through your analytical process during recorded sessions. The work flows on a recurring basis, allowing you to contribute flexibly as new scientific topics emerge.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for credentialed researchers holding a PhD in a core biological science. We welcome experts in Genetics, Protein Engineering, Biochemistry, and closely adjacent fields like Molecular Biology or Computational Biology. Ideal candidates have active experience working with complex datasets and analyzing recent scientific literature.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Review and analyze complex biological data sets or technical literature</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Provide detailed written feedback on emerging concepts in genetics and biochemistry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Participate in occasional remote interviews to explain your analytical reasoning</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate computational models applied to protein engineering</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">PhD in Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or a closely related field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in analyzing technical scientific literature</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable providing detailed, independent technical assessments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active experience in academic research or applied life sciences</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210 per task</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/fa6904f7-b04e-4430-9c17-ff13c9e673d6?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring biology PhDs to provide ongoing technical expertise in genetics, protein engineering, and biochemistry. This long-term research effort aims to evaluate complex biological data and map out emerging scientific trends. Your domain knowledge will directly support the evaluation of advanced computational biology models and literature reviews.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in remote tasks and occasional video interviews to evaluate technical biological concepts. Expect to review academic literature, analyze protein structures, or assess genetic data sets based on specific prompts. You will provide detailed written feedback and walk us through your analytical process during recorded sessions. The work flows on a recurring basis, allowing you to contribute flexibly as new scientific topics emerge.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for credentialed researchers holding a PhD in a core biological science. We welcome experts in Genetics, Protein Engineering, Biochemistry, and closely adjacent fields like Molecular Biology or Computational Biology. Ideal candidates have active experience working with complex datasets and analyzing recent scientific literature.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Review and analyze complex biological data sets or technical literature\n\n - Provide detailed written feedback on emerging concepts in genetics and biochemistry\n\n - Participate in occasional remote interviews to explain your analytical reasoning\n\n - Evaluate computational models applied to protein engineering\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - PhD in Biology, Genetics, Biochemistry, or a closely related field\n\n - Strong background in analyzing technical scientific literature\n\n - Comfortable providing detailed, independent technical assessments\n\n - Active experience in academic research or applied life sciences\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210 per task\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/fa6904f7-b04e-4430-9c17-ff13c9e673d6?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9d5dba8a-7dd2-4c21-8e95-9e17e6bdb764","title":"Full-Stack Engineers: Interview on Cybersecurity and CI/CD Pipelines","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Brazil","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T00:51:40.662+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Brazil"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/9d5dba8a-7dd2-4c21-8e95-9e17e6bdb764","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/9d5dba8a-7dd2-4c21-8e95-9e17e6bdb764/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the intersection of full-stack development and cybersecurity practices. Our goal is to understand how engineering teams balance feature development with robust vulnerability verification. This research will help refine tooling and processes for secure application deployment.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote technical interview to discuss your recent development projects. We will ask you to walk through your approach to managing CI/CD pipelines and integrating security checks. You will react to a few hypothetical deployment scenarios and explain how you verify vulnerabilities. The conversation will focus on your day-to-day workflow and technical decision-making process.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome full-stack engineers, application security engineers, and DevOps professionals with a strong cybersecurity background. You should have hands-on experience owning application features and securing deployment pipelines. Candidates who regularly perform vulnerability verification in production environments are an ideal fit for this conversation.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your process for integrating security into CI/CD pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe how you handle vulnerability verification during feature development</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">React to technical scenarios involving application security threats</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss your day-to-day workflow for balancing feature velocity with security requirements</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active full-stack engineer or application security professional</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in cybersecurity and threat management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience managing and securing CI/CD pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with vulnerability verification processes in production</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$55 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/fecf3792-b3b7-480b-816a-cd7d9758851c?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the intersection of full-stack development and cybersecurity practices. Our goal is to understand how engineering teams balance feature development with robust vulnerability verification. This research will help refine tooling and processes for secure application deployment.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote technical interview to discuss your recent development projects. We will ask you to walk through your approach to managing CI/CD pipelines and integrating security checks. You will react to a few hypothetical deployment scenarios and explain how you verify vulnerabilities. The conversation will focus on your day-to-day workflow and technical decision-making process.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome full-stack engineers, application security engineers, and DevOps professionals with a strong cybersecurity background. You should have hands-on experience owning application features and securing deployment pipelines. Candidates who regularly perform vulnerability verification in production environments are an ideal fit for this conversation.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Walk us through your process for integrating security into CI/CD pipelines\n\n - Describe how you handle vulnerability verification during feature development\n\n - React to technical scenarios involving application security threats\n\n - Discuss your day-to-day workflow for balancing feature velocity with security requirements\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active full-stack engineer or application security professional\n\n - Strong background in cybersecurity and threat management\n\n - Hands-on experience managing and securing CI/CD pipelines\n\n - Familiarity with vulnerability verification processes in production\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$55 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/fecf3792-b3b7-480b-816a-cd7d9758851c?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"278c9ea2-3a30-4a8a-b267-7844db8ff6a3","title":"Ocean Logistics Decision-Makers: Interview On Freight Operations","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"India","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T13:32:53.875+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"India"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/278c9ea2-3a30-4a8a-b267-7844db8ff6a3","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/278c9ea2-3a30-4a8a-b267-7844db8ff6a3/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the day-to-day realities of managing ocean logistics at scale. We want to understand how supply chain leaders handle shipping strategies, vendor relationships, and international route planning. This research directly informs how global shipping platforms design their future service offerings.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will complete a 60-minute remote interview guided by an AI moderator. During the session, you will discuss your typical logistics workflows and how you evaluate ocean carriers for your business. The AI will ask follow-up questions based on your specific operational setup and recent shipping challenges. You can complete this voice conversation at your own pace using your computer or mobile device.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for logistics decision-makers and supply chain influencers at medium-to-large technology and automotive companies. We welcome logistics managers, supply chain directors, and freight procurement specialists based in the IMEA region. Candidates should have direct experience working with major ocean carriers to route international freight.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Detail your approach to selecting and managing ocean freight vendors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through a recent supply chain challenge and how you resolved it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Answer AI-generated follow-up questions about your daily logistics workflows.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate current industry practices for international route planning.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience in ocean logistics or supply chain management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently employed in the technology or automotive sector</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with managing large-scale international freight routing</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable participating in an AI-moderated voice interview</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$257 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/06daf026-82ad-4bd4-8713-ec24089db3c7?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the day-to-day realities of managing ocean logistics at scale. We want to understand how supply chain leaders handle shipping strategies, vendor relationships, and international route planning. This research directly informs how global shipping platforms design their future service offerings.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will complete a 60-minute remote interview guided by an AI moderator. During the session, you will discuss your typical logistics workflows and how you evaluate ocean carriers for your business. The AI will ask follow-up questions based on your specific operational setup and recent shipping challenges. You can complete this voice conversation at your own pace using your computer or mobile device.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for logistics decision-makers and supply chain influencers at medium-to-large technology and automotive companies. We welcome logistics managers, supply chain directors, and freight procurement specialists based in the IMEA region. Candidates should have direct experience working with major ocean carriers to route international freight.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Detail your approach to selecting and managing ocean freight vendors.\n\n - Walk us through a recent supply chain challenge and how you resolved it.\n\n - Answer AI-generated follow-up questions about your daily logistics workflows.\n\n - Evaluate current industry practices for international route planning.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience in ocean logistics or supply chain management\n\n - Currently employed in the technology or automotive sector\n\n - Familiarity with managing large-scale international freight routing\n\n - Comfortable participating in an AI-moderated voice interview\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$257 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/06daf026-82ad-4bd4-8713-ec24089db3c7?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"2a057051-1b08-4bc0-994c-95cf0be49ca1","title":"Full-Stack Engineers (Cybersecurity): Feedback On CI/CD Workflows","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T02:41:37.340+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/2a057051-1b08-4bc0-994c-95cf0be49ca1","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/2a057051-1b08-4bc0-994c-95cf0be49ca1/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on the intersection of full-stack development and cybersecurity practices. Our goal is to understand how engineering teams integrate vulnerability verification directly into their CI/CD pipelines. This feedback will help shape future developer tools designed to streamline secure application feature ownership.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">During a remote video session, you will walk us through a recent project where you owned both application development and vulnerability verification. You will be asked to describe your current CI/CD setup, highlighting the specific steps you take to ensure secure deployments. We will then show you a few conceptual workflows and ask for your candid feedback on their practicality. The conversation flows as a standard technical interview, focusing on your day-to-day security routines.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We welcome full-stack engineers who have a dedicated focus or strong background in cybersecurity. You should have hands-on experience managing application features, configuring CI/CD pipelines, and verifying vulnerabilities prior to production. We also welcome DevSecOps engineers and security-focused backend developers who handle similar deployment pipelines.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your process for integrating vulnerability verification into CI/CD pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Discuss how you balance application feature development with rigorous security requirements</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">React to new concepts for managing and deploying secure full-stack applications</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe a recent challenge you faced while securing a production pipeline</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience as a full-stack engineer, DevSecOps engineer, or similar role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong background in cybersecurity and application security practices</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience configuring and maintaining CI/CD pipelines</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing vulnerability verification and secure deployment workflows</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$105 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/905d5706-56a4-4973-9736-73a30a3ca874?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on the intersection of full-stack development and cybersecurity practices. Our goal is to understand how engineering teams integrate vulnerability verification directly into their CI/CD pipelines. This feedback will help shape future developer tools designed to streamline secure application feature ownership.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nDuring a remote video session, you will walk us through a recent project where you owned both application development and vulnerability verification. You will be asked to describe your current CI/CD setup, highlighting the specific steps you take to ensure secure deployments. We will then show you a few conceptual workflows and ask for your candid feedback on their practicality. The conversation flows as a standard technical interview, focusing on your day-to-day security routines.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe welcome full-stack engineers who have a dedicated focus or strong background in cybersecurity. You should have hands-on experience managing application features, configuring CI/CD pipelines, and verifying vulnerabilities prior to production. We also welcome DevSecOps engineers and security-focused backend developers who handle similar deployment pipelines.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Walk us through your process for integrating vulnerability verification into CI/CD pipelines\n\n - Discuss how you balance application feature development with rigorous security requirements\n\n - React to new concepts for managing and deploying secure full-stack applications\n\n - Describe a recent challenge you faced while securing a production pipeline\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience as a full-stack engineer, DevSecOps engineer, or similar role\n\n - Strong background in cybersecurity and application security practices\n\n - Hands-on experience configuring and maintaining CI/CD pipelines\n\n - Comfortable discussing vulnerability verification and secure deployment workflows\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$105 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/905d5706-56a4-4973-9736-73a30a3ca874?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"32f70329-4dcc-490e-a265-9c9d58394834","title":"Practicing Clinicians: Paid Interview on Outpatient Care Workflows","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T04:34:56.620+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/32f70329-4dcc-490e-a265-9c9d58394834","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/32f70329-4dcc-490e-a265-9c9d58394834/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are running a paid study on clinical workflows within outpatient and community-based healthcare settings. Our goal is to map the realities of patient care delivery outside of traditional hospital environments. This research directly informs how modern clinical tools can better support day-to-day medical practice.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote voice and video interview moderated by our AI platform. During the session, you will describe your typical patient care routines and outline the steps you take to manage outpatient workflows. We will ask you to react to hypothetical clinical scenarios and share the operational hurdles you face most often. Your feedback will be collected through guided conversational prompts to capture a realistic picture of your practice.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for practicing clinicians who currently work in outpatient or community-based medical settings. We welcome primary care physicians, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, and specialist clinicians managing community clinics. You should have direct experience coordinating patient care workflows outside of a large inpatient hospital system.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe your daily clinical workflow in an outpatient setting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through how you manage routine patient care delivery</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Identify operational challenges or bottlenecks in your current practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Respond to AI-guided questions about community-based care scenarios</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Currently practicing as a clinician in an outpatient or community clinic</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct experience managing patient care delivery workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing the operational realities of your medical practice</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ability to join a remote video call from a quiet environment</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$210 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/93418896-7dfa-4d14-85e0-d00be2a536ec?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe are running a paid study on clinical workflows within outpatient and community-based healthcare settings. Our goal is to map the realities of patient care delivery outside of traditional hospital environments. This research directly informs how modern clinical tools can better support day-to-day medical practice.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote voice and video interview moderated by our AI platform. During the session, you will describe your typical patient care routines and outline the steps you take to manage outpatient workflows. We will ask you to react to hypothetical clinical scenarios and share the operational hurdles you face most often. Your feedback will be collected through guided conversational prompts to capture a realistic picture of your practice.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for practicing clinicians who currently work in outpatient or community-based medical settings. We welcome primary care physicians, nurse practitioners, physician assistants, and specialist clinicians managing community clinics. You should have direct experience coordinating patient care workflows outside of a large inpatient hospital system.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Describe your daily clinical workflow in an outpatient setting\n\n - Walk us through how you manage routine patient care delivery\n\n - Identify operational challenges or bottlenecks in your current practice\n\n - Respond to AI-guided questions about community-based care scenarios\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Currently practicing as a clinician in an outpatient or community clinic\n\n - Direct experience managing patient care delivery workflows\n\n - Comfortable discussing the operational realities of your medical practice\n\n - Ability to join a remote video call from a quiet environment\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$210 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/93418896-7dfa-4d14-85e0-d00be2a536ec?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"78837c0f-1322-4ced-87dc-63c71f6b094e","title":"Contact Center Professionals: Feedback on Speech Analytics Optimization","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T17:20:53.887+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/78837c0f-1322-4ced-87dc-63c71f6b094e","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/78837c0f-1322-4ced-87dc-63c71f6b094e/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on a new way to test and optimize topics in customer service software with speech analytics capabilities. Our goal is to streamline how teams manage phrase matching and intent detection. Your feedback will directly influence how these testing workflows are designed.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will participate in a remote video interview to walk us through your current speech analytics workflows. We will ask you to describe how you handle intent detection and topic optimization today. Then, you will review early concepts for a new testing interface and provide your honest reactions. Finally, we will discuss how these concepts compare to your existing tools.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for contact center and customer service professionals with hands-on experience in speech analytics. You should be familiar with phrase matching, topic optimization, or intent detection tools. We welcome call center managers, customer experience analysts, and speech analytics specialists.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through how you currently manage topics and intent detection</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Describe your workflow for testing phrase matching in customer service software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">React to early concepts for a new speech analytics optimization tool</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compare proposed testing methods with your current software solutions</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Active professional in a contact center or customer service environment</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on experience with speech analytics software</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with phrase matching or intent detection workflows</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable discussing technical aspects of topic optimization</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$25 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/61e768f7-980b-403a-ab6e-82b612cc9ad0?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on a new way to test and optimize topics in customer service software with speech analytics capabilities. Our goal is to streamline how teams manage phrase matching and intent detection. Your feedback will directly influence how these testing workflows are designed.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will participate in a remote video interview to walk us through your current speech analytics workflows. We will ask you to describe how you handle intent detection and topic optimization today. Then, you will review early concepts for a new testing interface and provide your honest reactions. Finally, we will discuss how these concepts compare to your existing tools.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for contact center and customer service professionals with hands-on experience in speech analytics. You should be familiar with phrase matching, topic optimization, or intent detection tools. We welcome call center managers, customer experience analysts, and speech analytics specialists.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Walk us through how you currently manage topics and intent detection\n\n - Describe your workflow for testing phrase matching in customer service software\n\n - React to early concepts for a new speech analytics optimization tool\n\n - Compare proposed testing methods with your current software solutions\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Active professional in a contact center or customer service environment\n\n - Hands-on experience with speech analytics software\n\n - Familiarity with phrase matching or intent detection workflows\n\n - Comfortable discussing technical aspects of topic optimization\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$25 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/61e768f7-980b-403a-ab6e-82b612cc9ad0?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"9f8d7438-ffd8-42be-b169-a46437154c79","title":"Machine Learning Engineers: Scenario Building for Reinforcement Learning","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T18:16:18.549+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/9f8d7438-ffd8-42be-b169-a46437154c79","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/9f8d7438-ffd8-42be-b169-a46437154c79/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're hiring AI researchers and machine learning engineers to participate in building worlds within a reinforcement learning platform. This work directly influences how agents interact with complex, simulated environments during their training cycles. Your technical expertise will help us refine the tools and interfaces used to create robust testing scenarios.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You will connect to our remote platform to design and construct specific scenarios for reinforcement learning agents. Throughout the session, you will configure environmental parameters, define spatial constraints, and run preliminary agent interactions to test your setup. You will document your workflow and note any friction points encountered while structuring the environment. Finally, you will participate in an interview to share your feedback on the platform's overall usability.</p><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This study targets professionals with hands-on experience in simulation design and reinforcement learning environments. We welcome machine learning engineers, AI researchers, simulation developers, and technical game designers accustomed to RL frameworks. Candidates should be highly comfortable configuring complex platform interfaces and defining structured agent scenarios.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Design and build specific scenarios within a remote reinforcement learning platform</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Configure environmental parameters and define agent interaction rules</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Test initial agent behaviors to validate your scenario structure</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Walk us through your workflow and highlight areas for platform improvement</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Professional experience in machine learning or artificial intelligence research</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Hands-on background in building simulations or reinforcement learning environments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with configuring platform interfaces and defining reward structures</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable articulating technical feedback during a remote interview</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$90 per hour</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/8b2a6e81-53d0-408e-b498-8fc46a15fdee?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're hiring AI researchers and machine learning engineers to participate in building worlds within a reinforcement learning platform. This work directly influences how agents interact with complex, simulated environments during their training cycles. Your technical expertise will help us refine the tools and interfaces used to create robust testing scenarios.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\nYou will connect to our remote platform to design and construct specific scenarios for reinforcement learning agents. Throughout the session, you will configure environmental parameters, define spatial constraints, and run preliminary agent interactions to test your setup. You will document your workflow and note any friction points encountered while structuring the environment. Finally, you will participate in an interview to share your feedback on the platform's overall usability.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nThis study targets professionals with hands-on experience in simulation design and reinforcement learning environments. We welcome machine learning engineers, AI researchers, simulation developers, and technical game designers accustomed to RL frameworks. Candidates should be highly comfortable configuring complex platform interfaces and defining structured agent scenarios.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Design and build specific scenarios within a remote reinforcement learning platform\n\n - Configure environmental parameters and define agent interaction rules\n\n - Test initial agent behaviors to validate your scenario structure\n\n - Walk us through your workflow and highlight areas for platform improvement\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Professional experience in machine learning or artificial intelligence research\n\n - Hands-on background in building simulations or reinforcement learning environments\n\n - Familiarity with configuring platform interfaces and defining reward structures\n\n - Comfortable articulating technical feedback during a remote interview\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$90 per hour\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/8b2a6e81-53d0-408e-b498-8fc46a15fdee?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}},{"id":"1becd726-a661-48fc-9cf6-3db388c79f42","title":"New Android Users: 30-Day Diary Study on Phone Setup (Germany)","department":"Participant Recruitment","team":"Participant Recruitment","employmentType":"Contract","location":"Germany","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":false,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-09-03T20:34:57.752+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"Germany"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/1becd726-a661-48fc-9cf6-3db388c79f42","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/terac/1becd726-a661-48fc-9cf6-3db388c79f42/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>What We're Researching</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're running a paid study on what it's actually like to set up and live with a brand-new Android phone. We want to understand where the first month goes smoothly and where it gets confusing — from unboxing and data migration to discovering features weeks later. This research feeds directly into how mobile operating systems guide people through setup.</p><h2>Please Read This Before Applying</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This study asks more of you than a typical survey. We would rather you know everything up front than discover it halfway through.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>You buy the phone yourself, and we reimburse you in full.</strong> You will purchase either a Google Pixel 11 or a Samsung Galaxy Z Flip8 between 28 September and 4 October 2026, in person at a Telekom, Vodafone or O2 store in Germany. You pay at the time of purchase. We reimburse the full device price in two payments. The $368 study compensation is separate and on top of that reimbursement.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The phone becomes your main phone for a month.</strong> You will transfer your SIM to the new device and use it as your primary phone for the duration of the study.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>The study needs some data from the device.</strong> You will install an app that provides the device identifiers, and keep \"Usage &amp; Diagnostics\" switched on in settings for the length of the study.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If any of that does not work for you, this is not the right study — and that is completely fine.</p><h2>How It Works</h2><ol style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You apply and complete a short screening questionnaire.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">If selected, you buy the phone between 28 September and 4 October 2026.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Between 28 September and 30 October you complete nine short diary entries, roughly 15 to 20 minutes each. You can answer in writing, or with photos, audio or video — whichever suits you.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Between 9 and 13 November you join one 60-minute remote interview over Zoom.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Your compensation is issued once your participation is approved.</p></li></ol><h2>Who This Is For</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are looking for everyday consumers in Germany, 18 or older, who were already thinking about buying a new phone. You should be the person who decides which phone you buy. You do not need to be technical — in fact, we specifically want people who are not.</p><h2>Who Cannot Take Part</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">People who work in UX, market research, or the technology industry</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Employees of large technology companies</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Anyone who has taken part in a market research study or focus group in the past few months</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$368 for full participation, plus full reimbursement of the phone's purchase price.</p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Buy a Google Pixel 11 or Samsung Galaxy Z Flip8 between 28 Sept and 4 Oct 2026, in store at Telekom, Vodafone or O2 (cost fully reimbursed)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Transfer your SIM and use the new phone as your primary device for about a month.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Complete nine short diary entries over 30 days, 15–20 minutes each.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join one 60-minute remote interview over Zoom between 9 and 13 November 2026.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Install an app providing the device identifiers and keep Usage &amp; Diagnostics enabled during the study.</p></li></ul><h2>Who Should Apply</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable documenting daily mobile usage and early impressions</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Live in Germany and be 18 or older.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Be the main decision maker for your own phone purchase.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willing to pay for the phone up front and be reimbursed in two payments</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Available for the full study period, from late September to mid November 2026.</p></li></ul><h2>Compensation</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$368 one-time</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>Ready to participate?</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com/interview/start/r/7576c5a8-57bf-4b1f-b1be-4dae402d15b5?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\"><strong>Start your paid interview now</strong></a></p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><h2>About Terac</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Terac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.</p><div style=\"min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0\"> </div><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Learn more at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://terac.com\">terac.com</a> or on YouTube at <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac\">@jointerac</a>.</p>","descriptionPlain":"WHAT WE'RE RESEARCHING\n\nWe're running a paid study on what it's actually like to set up and live with a brand-new Android phone. We want to understand where the first month goes smoothly and where it gets confusing — from unboxing and data migration to discovering features weeks later. This research feeds directly into how mobile operating systems guide people through setup.\n\n\nPLEASE READ THIS BEFORE APPLYING\n\nThis study asks more of you than a typical survey. We would rather you know everything up front than discover it halfway through.\n\nYou buy the phone yourself, and we reimburse you in full. You will purchase either a Google Pixel 11 or a Samsung Galaxy Z Flip8 between 28 September and 4 October 2026, in person at a Telekom, Vodafone or O2 store in Germany. You pay at the time of purchase. We reimburse the full device price in two payments. The $368 study compensation is separate and on top of that reimbursement.\n\nThe phone becomes your main phone for a month. You will transfer your SIM to the new device and use it as your primary phone for the duration of the study.\n\nThe study needs some data from the device. You will install an app that provides the device identifiers, and keep \"Usage & Diagnostics\" switched on in settings for the length of the study.\n\nIf any of that does not work for you, this is not the right study — and that is completely fine.\n\n\nHOW IT WORKS\n\n 1. You apply and complete a short screening questionnaire.\n\n 2. If selected, you buy the phone between 28 September and 4 October 2026.\n\n 3. Between 28 September and 30 October you complete nine short diary entries, roughly 15 to 20 minutes each. You can answer in writing, or with photos, audio or video — whichever suits you.\n\n 4. Between 9 and 13 November you join one 60-minute remote interview over Zoom.\n\n 5. Your compensation is issued once your participation is approved.\n\n\nWHO THIS IS FOR\n\nWe are looking for everyday consumers in Germany, 18 or older, who were already thinking about buying a new phone. You should be the person who decides which phone you buy. You do not need to be technical — in fact, we specifically want people who are not.\n\n\nWHO CANNOT TAKE PART\n\n - People who work in UX, market research, or the technology industry\n\n - Employees of large technology companies\n\n - Anyone who has taken part in a market research study or focus group in the past few months\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$368 for full participation, plus full reimbursement of the phone's purchase price.\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL DO\n\n - Buy a Google Pixel 11 or Samsung Galaxy Z Flip8 between 28 Sept and 4 Oct 2026, in store at Telekom, Vodafone or O2 (cost fully reimbursed)\n\n - Transfer your SIM and use the new phone as your primary device for about a month.\n\n - Complete nine short diary entries over 30 days, 15–20 minutes each.\n\n - Join one 60-minute remote interview over Zoom between 9 and 13 November 2026.\n\n - Install an app providing the device identifiers and keep Usage & Diagnostics enabled during the study.\n\n\nWHO SHOULD APPLY\n\n - Comfortable documenting daily mobile usage and early impressions\n\n - Live in Germany and be 18 or older.\n\n - Be the main decision maker for your own phone purchase.\n\n - Willing to pay for the phone up front and be reimbursed in two payments\n\n - Available for the full study period, from late September to mid November 2026.\n\n\nCOMPENSATION\n\n$368 one-time\n\n \n\n\nREADY TO PARTICIPATE?\n\nStart your paid interview now https://terac.com/interview/start/r/7576c5a8-57bf-4b1f-b1be-4dae402d15b5?utm_source=ashby_listing_description\n\n \n\n\nABOUT TERAC\n\nTerac is building the world's largest pool of vetted human experts for AI. Researchers, AI labs, and product teams use Terac to recruit, screen, and pay study participants across industries, languages, and skill sets.\n\n \n\nLearn more at terac.com https://terac.com or on YouTube at @jointerac https://www.youtube.com/@jointerac.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":null,"scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[],"summaryComponents":[]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}